.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt SSL_CTX_SET_RECORD_PADDING_CALLBACK 3ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm SSL_CTX_set_record_padding_callback ,
.Nm SSL_set_record_padding_callback ,
.Nm SSL_CTX_set_record_padding_callback_arg ,
.Nm SSL_set_record_padding_callback_arg ,
.Nm SSL_CTX_get_record_padding_callback_arg ,
.Nm SSL_get_record_padding_callback_arg ,
.Nm SSL_CTX_set_block_padding ,
.Nm SSL_CTX_set_block_padding_ex ,
.Nm SSL_set_block_padding ,
.Nm SSL_set_block_padding_ex
.Nd install callback to specify TLS 1.3 record padding
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In openssl/ssl.h
.Ft void
.Fo SSL_CTX_set_record_padding_callback
.Fa "SSL_CTX *ctx"
.Fa "size_t (*cb)(SSL *s"
.Fa "int type"
.Fa "size_t len"
.Fa "void *arg)"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo SSL_set_record_padding_callback
.Fa "SSL *ssl"
.Fa "size_t (*cb)(SSL *s"
.Fa "int type"
.Fa "size_t len"
.Fa "void *arg)"
.Fc
.Ft void
.Fo SSL_CTX_set_record_padding_callback_arg
.Fa "SSL_CTX *ctx"
.Fa "void *arg"
.Fc
.Ft void *
.Fo SSL_CTX_get_record_padding_callback_arg
.Fa "const SSL_CTX *ctx"
.Fc
.Ft void
.Fo SSL_set_record_padding_callback_arg
.Fa "SSL *ssl"
.Fa "void *arg"
.Fc
.Ft void *
.Fo SSL_get_record_padding_callback_arg
.Fa "const SSL *ssl"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo SSL_CTX_set_block_padding
.Fa "SSL_CTX *ctx"
.Fa "size_t block_size"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo SSL_set_block_padding
.Fa "SSL *ssl"
.Fa "size_t block_size"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo SSL_CTX_set_block_padding_ex
.Fa "SSL_CTX *ctx"
.Fa "size_t app_block_size"
.Fa "size_t hs_block_size"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo SSL_set_block_padding_ex
.Fa "SSL *ssl"
.Fa "size_t app_block_size"
.Fa "size_t hs_block_size"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn SSL_CTX_set_record_padding_callback
or
.Fn SSL_set_record_padding_callback
can be used to assign a callback function
.Em cb
to specify the padding for TLS 1.3 records.
The value set in
.Fa ctx
is copied to a new SSL by
.Xr SSL_new 3 .
Kernel TLS is not possible if the record padding callback is set, and
the callback function cannot be set if Kernel TLS is already configured
for the current SSL object.
.Pp
.Fn SSL_CTX_set_record_padding_callback_arg
and
.Fn SSL_set_record_padding_callback_arg
assign a value
.Fa arg
that is passed to the callback when it is invoked.
The value set in
.Fa ctx
is copied to a new SSL by
.Xr SSL_new 3 .
.Pp
.Fn SSL_CTX_get_record_padding_callback_arg
and
.Fn SSL_get_record_padding_callback_arg
retrieve the
.Fa arg
value that is passed to the callback.
.Pp
.Fn SSL_CTX_set_block_padding
and
.Fn SSL_set_block_padding
pads the record to a multiple of the
.Fa block_size .
A
.Fa block_size
of 0 or 1 disables block padding.
The limit of
.Fa block_size
is SSL3_RT_MAX_PLAIN_LENGTH.
.Pp
.Fn SSL_CTX_set_block_padding_ex
and
.Fn SSL_set_block_padding_ex
do similarly but allow the caller to separately specify the padding
block size to be applied to handshake and application data messages.
.Pp
The callback is invoked for every record before encryption.
The
.Fa type
parameter is the TLS record type that is being processed; may be one of
SSL3_RT_APPLICATION_DATA, SSL3_RT_HANDSHAKE, or SSL3_RT_ALERT. The
.Fa len
parameter is the current plaintext length of the record before
encryption.
The
.Fa arg
parameter is the value set via
.Fn SSL_CTX_set_record_padding_callback_arg
or
.Fn SSL_set_record_padding_callback_arg .
.Pp
These functions cannot be used with QUIC SSL objects.
.Fn SSL_set_record_padding_callback
and
.Fn SSL_set_block_padding
fail if called on a QUIC SSL object.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
The
.Fn SSL_CTX_get_record_padding_callback_arg
and
.Fn SSL_get_record_padding_callback_arg
functions return the
.Fa arg
value assigned in the corresponding set functions.
.Pp
The
.Fn SSL_CTX_set_block_padding
and
.Fn SSL_set_block_padding
functions return 1 on success or 0 if
.Fa block_size
is too large.
.Pp
The
.Sy cb
returns the number of padding bytes to add to the record.
A return of 0 indicates no padding will be added.
A return value that causes the record to exceed the maximum record size
(SSL3_RT_MAX_PLAIN_LENGTH) will pad out to the maximum record size.
.Pp
The
.Fn SSL_CTX_get_record_padding_callback_arg
function returns 1 on success or 0 if the callback function is not set
because Kernel TLS is configured for the SSL object.
.Sh NOTES
The default behavior is to add no padding to the record.
.Pp
A user-supplied padding callback function will override the behavior set
by
.Fn SSL_set_block_padding
or
.Fn SSL_CTX_set_block_padding .
Setting the user-supplied callback to NULL will restore the configured
block padding behavior.
.Pp
These functions only apply to TLS 1.3 records being written.
.Pp
Padding bytes are not added in constant-time.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ssl 7 ,
.Xr SSL_new 3
.Sh HISTORY
The record padding API was added for TLS 1.3 support in OpenSSL 1.1.1.
.Pp
The return type of
.Fn SSL_CTX_set_record_padding_callback
function was changed to int in OpenSSL 3.0.
.Pp
The functions
.Fn SSL_set_block_padding_ex
and
.Fn SSL_CTX_set_block_padding_ex
were added in OpenSSL 3.4.
